Thanks to all who replied!  I'm sorry that I wasn't able to try the
recommendations out sooner, but I wasn't able to access the machine other
than remotely for a few days.

I did solve the problem by using Jeff Layton's much-appreciated
lvm2create_initrd script that he sent out recently.  However I did try out a
few more things before that that I thought to reply on for posterity...

First I checked the lvm.conf file and masked out all "^hd" entries with the
filter option.
	filter = [ "r/^hd/" ]

I also double-checked that the --ignorelockingfailure option was passed to
the vgchange command:
	/sbin/lvm vgchange --ignorelockingfailure -P -a y

I still got the same error when rebooting, however.  I did not try the
--mknodes option with vgscan, as was suggested, since the problem had
already been fixed with the initrd image generated by Mr. Layton's script (I
did both of these in one "step").  I may try the --mknodes option when I get
a chance later just to see if that works and will let everyone know if it
does.

Thanks again,
    Geoff





